[DOCUMENT]
TITLE: Hardware Requirements
PREFIX: HW-
OPTIONS:
  ENABLE_MID: True

[GRAMMAR]
ELEMENTS:
- TAG: REQUIREMENT
  FIELDS:
  - TITLE: UID
    TYPE: String
    REQUIRED: False
  - TITLE: TITLE
    TYPE: String
    REQUIRED: False
  - TITLE: STATEMENT
    TYPE: String
    REQUIRED: False
  - TITLE: COMPLETION_CRITERIA
    TYPE: String
    REQUIRED: False
  RELATIONS:
  - TYPE: Parent

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: HW-1
TITLE: Core compute module
STATEMENT: >>>
The board shall be built around a compute module powerful enough to render graphics, stream audio over Wifi, accept inputs, and manage peripherals simultaneously.
<<<
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: SYS-1

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: HW-2
TITLE: Display
STATEMENT: >>>
The board shall include a display connector routed for a TFT panel capable of rendering a smooth, detailed map view, driven over the SPI interface defined in I-1.
<<<
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: SYS-1

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: HW-3
TITLE: Audio output path
STATEMENT: >>>
The board shall include an audio output path (DAC or I2S) feeding a stereo amplifier and the built-in speakers, per the interface defined in I-2.
<<<
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: SYS-3

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: HW-4
TITLE: Map input mechanism
STATEMENT: >>>
The board shall provide an input mechanism suitable for pan/zoom map interaction. Input method (touch overlay, rotary encoder, physical buttons) is TBD -- see open questions.
<<<
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: SYS-1

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: HW-5
TITLE: Enclosure
STATEMENT: >>>
The enclosure shall house the display, speakers, and input hardware in a single self-contained form factor.
<<<
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: SYS-4